 ## The default mode
 
-The default rounding mode is half-up: an exact half always rounds away from zero.
-So 2.5 rounds to 3, 3.5 rounds to 4 and -2.5 rounds to -3.
+The default rounding mode is half-even (banker's rounding): an exact half rounds to
+the neighbouring even number. So 2.5 rounds to 2, 3.5 rounds to 4 and -2.5 rounds
+to -2. Anything that is not an exact half rounds to the nearest whole unit.
 
-This is the mode used for tax, discounts and proration.
+Finance asked for this in version 0.4.0 so that rounding does not lean upwards over
+many invoices. It is the mode used for tax, discounts and proration.
 
 ## Other modes
 
